{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778979946014,"sessionID":"ses_1cc885b9fffe3OQbM3nZ0uAKXI","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"skill","callID":"call_kk9PfOrIYT17bgDfWmCKmIZ4","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"name":"task-coordinator"},"output":"<skill_content name=\"task-coordinator\">\n# Skill: task-coordinator\n\nYou are the MONDO Ontology Task Coordinator, a master planner responsible for orchestrating all ontology work in the MONDO project. You MUST be used first for ANY ontology task to ensure proper planning, execution, and validation.\n\nYour core responsibilities:\n\n1. **Task Analysis & Decomposition**: Break down complex ontology requests into logical, sequential steps. Consider all aspects: research needs, design patterns, validation requirements, and potential risks.\n\n2. **Agent Orchestration**: Plan the optimal sequence of specialized agents:\n   - Start with deep-research-specialist for literature review when PMIDs are mentioned\n   - Use design-pattern-advisor to ensure compliance with MONDO patterns\n   - Coordinate execution agents for the actual ontology work\n   - Always include identifier-validator to prevent hallucinated IDs\n   - End with obo-checkin for term integration\n   - Use ontology-reasoner when logical definitions are involved\n\n3. **Critical Validation Oversight**: You are the final safeguard against:\n   - Hallucinated MONDO IDs, PMIDs, or gene identifiers\n   - Missing required metadata (definitions, sources, proper citations)\n   - Violations of MONDO naming conventions\n   - Incomplete check-in processes\n\n4. **Quality Assurance Protocol**: Ensure every task includes:\n   - Proper literature research when references are provided\n   - Design pattern compliance checking\n   - Identifier validation (especially for genes using HGNC or NCBI gene)\n   - Complete source attribution\n   - Syntax validation before check-in\n   - Reasoner validation for logical definitions\n\n5. **Risk Management**: Flag high-risk scenarios:\n   - New term creation without proper research\n   - Obsolescence without replacement planning\n   - Missing or incorrect gene identifiers\n   - Inadequate source citations\n\nYour planning output should specify:\n- The exact sequence of agents to use\n- Key validation checkpoints\n- Specific risks to monitor\n- Required deliverables at each step\n\nNEVER allow any ontology work to proceed without proper planning, validation, and check-in procedures. You are responsible for maintaining the integrity and quality of the MONDO ontology through systematic coordination of all specialized agents.\n\nBase directory for this skill: file:///__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/.claude/skills/task-coordinator\nRelative paths in this skill (e.g., scripts/, reference/) are relative to this base directory.\nNote: file list is sampled.\n\n<skill_files>\n\n</skill_files>\n</skill_content>","metadata":{"name":"task-coordinator","dir":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/.claude/skills/task-coordinator","truncated":false},"title":"Loaded skill: task-coordinator","time":{"start":1778979945947,"end":1778979946011}},"id":"prt_e3377bdcf0016XrTni54CWy9AR","sessionID":"ses_1cc885b9fffe3OQbM3nZ0uAKXI","messageID":"msg_e3377a57c001iznR06em7Yekl9"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778979946035,"sessionID":"ses_1cc885b9fffe3OQbM3nZ0uAKXI","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_63szi6VgPEQkx6OsLdqR65RB","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/__issue_context__.json","offset":1,"limit":400},"output":"<path>/__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/__issue_context__.json</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\n2:   \"body\": \"**Preferred gene-related syndrome label**\\nRNU12 - related minor spliceopathy disorder\\n\\n**Synonyms**\\ncraniosynostosis-anal anomalies-porokeratosis syndrome MONDO:0011287\\nCDAGS syndrome\\nspinocerebellar ataxia, autosomal recessive 33 MONDO:0859360 \\n\\n**Parent term (use [OLS](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/mondo), or your favorite ontology browser)**\\nhereditary disease, syndromic disease\\n\\n**Definition**\\nAbnormal splicing of pre-mRNA caused by variants in the RNU12 gene. This term captures the disease spectrum. The term includes craniosynostosis-anal anomalies-porokeratosis, also known as CDAGS syndrome, and spinocerebellar ataxia, autosomal recessive 33.\\n\\n\\n**Definition source (Please give PubMed ID, if applicable, in format PMID:#######)\\nPMID: 39802771\\n\\n**Children terms (if applicable)** Should any existing terms be re-classified as children underneath this new proposed term? \\ncraniosynostosis-anal anomalies-porokeratosis syndrome MONDO:0011287\\nspinocerebellar ataxia, autosomal recessive 33 MONDO:0859360\\n\\n**Your nano-attribution (ORCID) or URL for a working group**\\nhttps://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40060/\\n\",\n3:   \"comments\": [\n4:     {\n5:       \"id\": \"IC_kwDOBjach875FUee\",\n6:       \"author\": {\n7:         \"login\": \"vgitau\"\n8:       },\n9:       \"authorAssociation\": \"NONE\",\n10:       \"body\": \"Dear @sabrinatoro, I'm following up regarding the RNU12 request. Please let me know if you have any questions regarding the ClinGen preferred label