 ontological children are discovered, it is possible that this term might be merged with its single child. (https://clinicalgenome.org/working-groups/clinical-domain/ocular-cdwg/)\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0027249\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"BBS5-related ciliopathy\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/working-groups/clinical-domain/ocular-cdwg] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nxref: GARD:0027249 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0005308 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/working-groups/clinical-domain/ocular-cdwg/\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5935-2391\"} ! ciliopathy\nintersection_of: MONDO:0005308 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/working-groups/clinical-domain/ocular-cdwg/\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5935-2391\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693\"} ! ciliopathy\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/970 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/working-groups/clinical-domain/ocular-cdwg/\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5935-2391\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693\"} ! BBS5\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/7923\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1040066\nname: REEP6-related retinopathy\ndef: \"Any retinopathy caused by variants in the REEP6 gene.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/working-groups/clinical-domain/ocular-cdwg/, https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5935-2391, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693]\ncomment: REEP6-related retinopathy exhibits a spectrum of phenotypes that have yet to be formally defined, with the exception of retinitis pigmentosa 77. Thus it is placed as an only child.\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028147\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"REEP6-related retinopathy\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/working-groups/clinical-domain/ocular-cdwg/, https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5935-2391] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nxref: GARD:0028147 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0019118 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/working-groups/clinical-domain/ocular-cdwg/\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5935-2391\"} ! inherited retinal dystrophy\nintersection_of: MONDO:0019118 ! inherited retinal dystrophy\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/30078 ! REEP6\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8986\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060108\nname: PURA-related severe neonatal hypotonia-seizures-encephalopathy syndrome\ndef: \"A rare neurologic disease characterized by neonatal hypotonia, global developmental delay, feeding difficulties, and often seizures or seizure-like episodes. Other frequently observed signs and symptoms include variable dysmorphic features, myopathic facies, respiratory problems, and visual abnormalities, such as strabismus or esotropia. Brain imaging may show delayed myelination and other white matter abnormalities.\" [Orphanet:438213]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0027440\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: ordo_disorder {source=\"Orphanet:438213\"}\nsubset: orphanet {source=\"Orphanet:438213\"}\nsubset: orphanet_rare {source=\"Orphanet:438213\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"PURA syndrome\" NARROW [PMID:28448108]\nsynonym: \"PURA-related neurodevelopmental disorders\" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163, PMID:28448108]\nxref: GARD:0027440 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nxref: ICD10CM:G40.4 {source=\"Orphanet:438213\"}\nxref: MEDGEN:863794 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: Orphanet:438213 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: UMLS:C4015357 {source=\"MEDGEN:863794\", source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0003847 {source=\"PMID:28448108\"} ! hereditary disease\nis_a: MONDO:0015159 {source=\"Orphanet:438213\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163\"} ! multiple congenital anomalies/dysmorphic syndrome-intellectual disability\nrelationship: curated_content_resource https://www.malacards.org/card/pura_related_neurodevelopmental_disorders {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nrelationship: has_characteristic HP:0000006 {source=\"Orphanet:438213\"} ! Autosomal dominant inheritance\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/5114\" xsd:anyURI\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/6695\" xsd:anyURI\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/6752\" xsd:anyURI\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/6876\" xsd:anyURI\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/6878\" xsd:anyURI\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8953\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060109\nname: PLEC-related muscular dystrophy-epidermolysis bullosa simplex spectrum disorder\ndef: \"A spectrum of disease associated with loss or disrupted function of the PLEC gene. These disorders primarily affect the skin and muscles, leading to a range of symptoms including skin blistering (EBS), progressive muscle weakness (muscular dystrophy), and other complications.\" [PMID:35815343]\nsynonym: \"PLEC-related muscular dystrophy-epidermolysis bullosa simplex spectrum disorder\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40151/, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2078-7280, PMID:35815343] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nsynonym: \"qualitative or quantitative defects of plectin\" NARROW []\nis_a: MONDO:0003847 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40151/\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153\"} ! hereditary disease\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/9069 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40151/\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2078-7280\"} ! PLEC\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8951\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060110\nname: HDAC4-related haploinsufficiency syndrome\ndef: \"A disorder caused by haploinsufficiency of HDAC4 and is characterized by brachydactyly type E, variable mild to moderate intellectual disability, seizures, autism spectrum disorder, short stature, obesity, and facial dysmorphism. Individuals with the gain of functions variants typically do not have brachydactyly and do have more consistent intellectual disability.\" [https://www.clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40006/, PMID:33537682]\ncomment: This term is more specific because it includes brachydactyly that is not characterized in the parent term. https://www.clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40006/\nsynonym: \"brachydactyly intellectual disability syndrome\" BROAD [https://www.clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40006/]\nsynonym: \"brachydactyly mental retardation syndrome\" BROAD DEPRECATED [https://www.clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40006/]\nsynonym: \"HDAC4-related haploinsufficiency syndrome\" EXACT [https://www.clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40006/, PMID:33537682] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0859232 {source=\"https://www.clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40006/\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder with central hypotonia and dysmorphic facies\nrelationship: excluded_from_qc_check http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/mondo/sparql/qc/general/qc-single-child.sparql\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8897\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060111\nname: SAMD9L-related spectrum and myeloid neoplasm risk\ndef: \"A susceptibility or predisposition to myeloid neoplasms in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the SAMD9L gene. This condition is characterized by variable presentations of ataxia and cytopenia, myelodysplastic syndrome, monosomy 7 (acute myelogenous leukemia), and bone marrow failure.\" [MONDO:patterns/susceptibility_by_gene, PMID:29535429]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028150\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"SAMD9L-related spectrum and myeloid neoplasm risk\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/, https://orcid.org/0009-0004-3069-7846] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nxref: GARD:0028150 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0020573 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! inherited disease susceptibility\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/1349 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! SAMD9L\nrelationship: predisposes_towards MONDO:0008038 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! ataxia-pancytopenia syndrome\nrelationship: predisposes_towards MONDO:0018881 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! myelodysplastic syndrome\nrelationship: predisposes_towards MONDO:0044645 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! familial monosomy 7 syndrome\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8947\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060117\nname: MYCBP2-related developmental delay with corpus callosum defects\ndef: \"Any neurodevelopmental disorder in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the MYCBP2 gene. This condition is characterized by variable corpus callosum defects consistent with dysgenesis, and a broad spectrum of neurobehavioural deficits including developmental delay, intellectual disability, epilepsy, and autistic features.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163, PMID:36200388]\nsynonym: \"MDCD\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [PMID:36200388]\nsynonym: \"MYCBP2-related developmental delay with corpus callosum defects\" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163, PMID:36200388]\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"PMID:36200388\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: MONDO:0700092 ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/23386 ! MYCBP2\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/23386 {source=\"PMID:36200388\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163\"} ! MYCBP2\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9033\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060123\nname: GRIN1-related complex neurodevelopmental disorder\ndef: \"A neurodevelopmental disorder caused by variation in the GRIN1 gene. It is characterized by mild-to-profound developmental delay/intellectual disability (DD/ID) in all affected individuals. Other common manifestations are epilepsy, muscular hypotonia, movement disorders, spasticity, feeding difficulties, and behavior issues. A subset of individuals show a malformation of cortical development consisting of extensive and diffuse bilateral polymicrogyria.\" [PMID:31219694]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028154\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"GRIN1-related developmental and epileptic encephalopathy\" EXACT [PMID:31219694]\nsynonym: \"GRIN1-related neurodevelopmental disorder\" EXACT [PMID:31219694]\nxref: GARD:0028154 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"PMID:31219694\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nis_a: MONDO:1060138 {source=\"PMID:40374652\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163\"} ! GRIN-related complex neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: MONDO:0700092 ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/4584 ! GRIN1\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/4584 {source=\"PMID:31219694\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163\"} ! GRIN1\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9063\" xsd:string\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060138\nname: GRIN-related complex neurodevelopmental disorder\ndef: \"A group of neurological and neurodevelopmental disorders caused by pathogenic variants in genes encoding subunits of the N-methyl-D-aspartate (NMDA) receptor, including GRIN1, GRIN2A, GRIN2B, and GRIN2D. These disorders are associated with a spectrum of symptoms such as developmental delay, intellectual disability, epilepsy, movement disorders, speech and language impairment, and neuropsychiatric features. The clinical presentation and severity vary depending on the specific gene and mutation involved.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163, PMID:40374652]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028156\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"GRIN-related encephalopathy\" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163, PMID:38380699]\nsynonym: \"GRIN-related neurodevelopmental disorder\" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163, PMID:38727899]\nsynonym: \"GRINpathies\" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163, PMID:34884460]\nxref: GARD:0028156 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0003847 {source=\"PMID:40374652\"} ! hereditary disease\nis_a: MONDO:0100038 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153\"} ! complex neurodevelopmental disorder\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9063\" xsd:anyURI\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9930\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060139\nname: GRIN2A-related complex neurodevelopmental disorder\ndef: \"A group of neurological and neurodevelopmental disorders caused by variants in the GRIN2A gene, characterized by a broad spectrum of symptoms including developmental delay or intellectual disability, epilepsy, speech and language impairments, movement disorders, and neuropsychiatric features.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163, OMIM:245570, PMID:27683935]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028157\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nxref: GARD:0028157 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:1060138 {source=\"PMID:40374652\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163\"} ! GRIN-related complex neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: MONDO:0003847 ! hereditary disease\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/4585 ! GRIN2A\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/4585 {source=\"PMID:27683935\"} ! GRIN2A\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9063\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060140\nname: GRIN2A-related developmental and/or epileptic encephalopathy with spike-wave activation in sleep\ndef: \"Any developmental and/or epileptic encephalopathy with spike-wave activation in sleep in which the cause of the disease is a variation in GRIN2A gene.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163, MONDO:patterns/disease_series_by_gene, PMID:27683935]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028158\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nxref: GARD:0028158 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0800501 {source=\"PMID:27683935\"} ! developmental and/or epileptic encephalopathy with spike-wave activation in sleep\nis_a: MONDO:1060139 {source=\"PMID:27683935\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163\"} ! GRIN2A-related complex neurodevelopmental disorder\nrelationship: excluded_from_qc_check http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/mondo/sparql/qc/general/qc-single-child.sparql\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/4585 {source=\"PMID:27683935\"} ! GRIN2A\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9063\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060141\nname: GRIN2A-related rolandic epilepsy-speech dyspraxia syndrome\ndef: \"Any rolandic epilepsy-speech dyspraxia syndrome in which the cause of the disease is a variation in GRIN2A gene.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163, MONDO:patterns/disease_series_by_gene, PMID:27683935]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028159\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nxref: GARD:0028159 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0015587 {source=\"PMID:27683935\"} ! rolandic epilepsy-speech dyspraxia syndrome\nis_a: MONDO:1060139 {source=\"PMID:27683935\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163\"} ! GRIN2A-related complex neurodevelopmental disorder\nrelationship: excluded_from_qc_check http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/mondo/sparql/qc/general/qc-single-child.sparql\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/4585 {source=\"PMID:27683935\"} ! GRIN2A\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9063\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060142\nname: GRIN2A-related self-limited epilepsy with centrotemporal spikes\ndef: \"Any self-limited epilepsy with centrotemporal spikes in which the cause of the disease is a variation in GRIN2A gene.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163, MONDO:patterns/disease_series_by_gene, PMID:27683935]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028160\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nxref: GARD:0028160 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0007295 {source=\"PMID:27683935\"} ! self-limited epilepsy with centrotemporal spikes\nis_a: MONDO:1060139 {source=\"PMID:27683935\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163\"} ! GRIN2A-related complex neurodevelopmental disorder\nrelationship: excluded_from_qc_check http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/mondo/sparql/qc/general/qc-single-child.sparql\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/4585 {source=\"PMID:27683935\"} ! GRIN2A\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9063\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060148\nname: empty nose syndrome\ndef: \"A rare iatrogenic disease characterized by paradoxical nasal obstruction and symptoms including air hunger and suffocation-like breathing sensation, nasal dryness and crusting, burning pain or cold airflow sensation, impaired sleep and cognitive function and severe anxiety and depression, and typically occurs after surgical reduction or removal of nasal turbinates.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163, PMID:27557473, PMID:39126290]\ncomment: ENS is often misdiagnosed as psychiatric in origin due to the disproportionate suffering compared to physical exam findings. ENS results from disruption of normal nasal airflow dynamics, mucosal sensory feedback, and humidification, typically after aggressive surgical intervention on the nasal turbinates. Estimated prevalence: <1 in 10,000, though underreporting and misdiagnosis likely make this an underestimate. ENS is currently considered a rare, post-surgical complication, with cases reported globally but concentrated among ENT surgical patients. No universally accepted biomarker exists. Diagnosis is based on symptoms, medical history and imaging. There is no cure. Symptom management includes nasal moisturization (saline gels, humidification), nerve modulating agents (e.g., amitriptyline, gabapentin) nasal implants to restore airflow resistance and cognitive-behavioral therapy and psychiatric support. ENS most often develops after surgery and is considered an iatrogenic condition because its other causes also result from medical interventions, such as electrocautery or laser procedures that cause turbinate trauma.\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028165\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: mondo_curated_rare {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\", source=\"PMID:35155777\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"ENS\" EXACT [PMID:27557473, PMID:39126290]\nsynonym: \"nasal iatrogenic dysfunction\" BROAD [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163]\nsynonym: \"post-turbinectomy syndrome\" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163, PMID:17875850]\nsynonym: \"secondary atrophic rhinitis\" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163, PMID:35155777]\nxref: GARD:0028165 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nxref: MEDGEN:1876481 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: UMLS:C3888849 {source=\"MEDGEN:1876481\", source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0005659 {source=\"PMID:35155777\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163\"} ! atrophic rhinitis\nis_a: MONDO:0043543 {source=\"PMID:17875850\", source=\"PMID:27557473\", source=\"PMID:38961700\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163\"} ! iatrogenic disease\nrelationship: excluded_from_qc_check http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/mondo/sparql/qc/general/qc-single-child.sparql\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9174\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060149\nname: ACAN-related short stature spectrum\ndef: \"A rare semidominant genetic skeletal disorder caused by a variation in ACAN gene, characterized by short stature with variable phenotypic features which may include osteochondritis dissecans, advanced bone age, early-onset arthritis, and/or features consistent with spondyloepiphyseal dysplasia, Kimberley type caused by a single allele whereas biallelic variation can cause spondyloepimetaphyseal dysplasia, aggrecan type.\" [PMID:27311816, PMID:35434101]\nis_a: MONDO:0005381 {source=\"PMID:35434101\"} ! bone disorder\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/319 {source=\"PMID:35434101\"} ! ACAN\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9249\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060150\nname: NOTCH1-related AOS spectrum disorder\ndef: \"A disease characterized by a spectrum of cardiac and extracardiac phenotypes caused by a disease-causing variant in the NOTCH1 gene, inherited in an autosomal dominant manner. Affected individuals may present with congenital heart defects, bicuspid aortic valve, aortic valve stenosis, thoracic aortic aneurysm or dissection, anomalies in brain structure, intracranial or posterior circulation vascular anomalies, cutaneous vascular malformations, cutis marmorata, and/or a phenotype compatible with Adams-Oliver syndrome (i.e. cutis aplasia, terminal limb defects, skull ossification defects).\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40104/, https://orcid.org/0009-0007-6180-2639, PMID:25963545]\ncomment: Variants in NOTCH1 have been reported in individuals with the following disease entities: Adams-Oliver Syndrome, congenital heart disease, aortic valve disease including bicuspid aortic valve, and thoracic aortic aneurysm and dissection. Individuals with pathogenic variants in NOTCH1 may also be asymptomatic due to incomplete penetrance and extensive intrafamilial variability. Per criteria outlined by the ClinGen Lumping and Splitting guidelines, we found no difference in molecular mechanism and inheritance pattern and found considerable interfamilial and intrafamilial variability in cardiac phenotypes. Therefore, Adams-Oliver syndrome 5 and aortic valve disease 1 have been lumped into one disease entity (NOTCH1-related AOS spectrum disorder).\nis_a: MONDO:0002254 {source=\"PMID:25963545\", source=\"PMID:38778082\"} ! syndromic disease\nis_a: MONDO:0005453 {source=\"PMID:38778082\", source=\"PMID:40127276\", source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40104/\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0009-0007-6180-2639\"} ! congenital heart disease\nrelationship: has_characteristic HP:0000006 {source=\"PMID:25963545\", source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40104/\"} ! Autosomal dominant inheritance\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/7881 {source=\"PMID:25963545\", source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40104/\"} ! NOTCH1\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9236\" xsd:string\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9832\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060165\nname: ELANE-related neutropenia\ndef: \"Any neutropenia in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the ELANE gene.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163, MONDO:patterns/disease_series_by_gene]\ncomment: ELANE-related neutropenia includes congenital neutropenia and cyclic neutropenia, both of which are primary hematologic disorders characterized by recurrent fever, skin and oropharyngeal inflammation (i.e., mouth ulcers, gingivitis, sinusitis, and pharyngitis), and cervical adenopathy. Infectious complications are generally more severe in congenital neutropenia than in cyclic neutropenia.\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028170\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nxref: GARD:0028170 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0001475 {source=\"PMID:20301705\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163\"} ! neutropenia\nintersection_of: MONDO:0001475 ! neutropenia\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/3309 ! ELANE\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/3309 {source=\"PMID:20301705\"} ! ELANE\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9459\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060173\nname: FLNB-associated autosomal dominant filamin related bone disorder\ndef: \"Any autosomal dominant filamin related bone disorder in which the cause of the disease is a variation in FLNB gene.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40106/, MONDO:patterns/disease_series_by_gene, PMID:16752402, PMID:16801345, PMID:22190451, PMID:22354125]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028175\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"FLNB-associated autosomal dominant filamin related bone disorder\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40106/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nxref: GARD:0028175 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0000426 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40106/\"} ! autosomal dominant disease\nis_a: MONDO:0019690 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40106/\"} ! filamin-related bone disorder\nintersection_of: MONDO:0000426 ! autosomal dominant disease\nintersection_of: MONDO:0019690 ! filamin-related bone disorder\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/3755 ! FLNB\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/3755 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40106/\"} ! FLNB\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9528\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060179\nname: RNU5B-1 related neurodevelopmental disorder with seizures and joint laxity\ndef: \"A neurodevelopmental disorder in which the cause of the disease is a variation in RNU5B-1 gene and is characterized by global developmental delay, hypotonia, macrocephaly, failure to thrive, abnormality of the eye, seizures, and joint laxity\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40060/, MONDO:patterns/disease_series_by_gene, PMID:40379786, PMID:40442284]\nsubset: omim {source=\"OMIM:621302\"}\nsynonym: \"NEDSJL\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [OMIM:621302]\nsynonym: \"neurodevelopmental disorder with seizures and joint laxity\" EXACT [OMIM:621302]\nsynonym: \"RNU5B-1 related neurodevelopmental disorder with seizures and joint laxity\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40060/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nsynonym: \"RNU5B-1-related disorder\" BROAD [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40060/]\nxref: OMIM:621302 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0100500 {source=\"PMID:40379786\", source=\"PMID:40442284\", source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40060/\"} ! Mendelian neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: MONDO:0100500 ! Mendelian neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/10212 ! RNU5B-1\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/10212 {source=\"OMIM:621302\", source=\"PMID:40379786\", source=\"PMID:40442284\", source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40060/\"} ! RNU5B-1\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator \"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\" xsd:string\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9596\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060190\nname: APP-related brain and vascular amyloidosis\ndef: \"A hereditary amyloidosis characterized by a spectrum of neurodegenerative and neurovascular phenotypes caused by pathogenic variant in the APP gene, resulting in an abnormal clearance of amyloid peptides, either by overproduction and decreased clearance of amyloid peptides, with deposition of amyloid in plaques and blood vessel walls. Affected individuals may present with progressive cognitive decline, cerebral vascular amyloidosis with white matter changes, and stroke with or without hemorrhage.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40156/]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028185\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"APP-related brain and vascular amyloidosis\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40156/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nxref: GARD:0028185 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0011057 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40156/\"} ! cerebrovascular disorder\nis_a: MONDO:0018634 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40156/\"} ! hereditary amyloidosis\nis_a: MONDO:0024237 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40156/\"} ! inherited neurodegenerative disorder\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/620 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40156/\"} ! APP\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9721\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060192\nname: CASK-related intellectual disability\ndef: \"A syndromic disorder in which the cause of the disease is a variation in the CASK gene. It is associated with a wide phenotypic spectrum ranging from mild-to-severe intellectual disability with or without nystagmus to moderate-to-profound intellectual disability and progressive microcephaly with pontine and cerebellar hypoplasia, often associated with seizures.\" [MONDO:patterns/disease_series_by_gene, PMID:24278995]\nsynonym: \"CASK-related disorder\" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163, PMID:24278995]\nis_a: MONDO:0002254 {source=\"PMID:24278995\"} ! syndromic disease\nis_a: MONDO:0020119 {source=\"PMID:24278995\"} ! X-linked syndromic intellectual disability\nintersection_of: MONDO:0000508 ! syndromic intellectual disability\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/1497 ! CASK\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9747\" xsd:string\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060194\nname: FAS-related autoimmune lymphoproliferative immune disorder\ndef: \"An autoimmune lymphoproliferative syndrome that results from defective lymphocyte homoestasis, and is caused by variants in the FAS gene. It is characterized by non-malignant lymphoproliferation, autoimmune disease, and lifelong increased risk for both Hodgkin and non-Hodgkin lymphoma.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028187\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"FAS-related autoimmune lymphoproliferative immune disorder\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nxref: GARD:0028187 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0017979 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! autoimmune lymphoproliferative syndrome\nintersection_of: MONDO:0017979 ! autoimmune lymphoproliferative syndrome\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/11920 ! FAS\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/11920 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! FAS\nrelationship: predisposes_towards MONDO:0004952 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! Hodgkins lymphoma\nrelationship: predisposes_towards MONDO:0018908 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! non-Hodgkin lymphoma\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9749\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060195\nname: SH2B3-related immune system disorder\ndef: \"A predisposition caused by a mutation in SH2B3 gene that presents with myeloproliferation and/or multi-organ autoimmunity.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/]\nsynonym: \"SH2B3-related immune system disorder\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nsynonym: \"SH2B3-related myeloproliferation and autoimmunity\" RELATED [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/]\nis_a: MONDO:0020573 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! inherited disease susceptibility\nintersection_of: MONDO:0020573 ! inherited disease susceptibility\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/29605 ! SH2B3\nintersection_of: predisposes_towards MONDO:0005046 ! immune system disorder\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/29605 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! SH2B3\nrelationship: predisposes_towards MONDO:0005046 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! immune system disorder\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9576\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060199\nname: hemorrhagic stroke\ndef: \"A stroke disorder caused by bleeding into the brain parenchyma or surrounding spaces. Hemorrhagic stroke includes intracerebral hemorrhage (bleeding within the brain tissue) and subarachnoid hemorrhage (bleeding in the space between the brain and the surrounding membrane).\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767, https://www.hopkinsmedicine.org/health/conditions-and-diseases/stroke/types-of-stroke, https://www.stroke.org.uk/stroke/types, PMID:29763173]\nsubset: doid {source=\"DOID:0051063\"}\nsynonym: \"haemorrhagic stroke\" EXACT OMO:0003005 []\nxref: DOID:0051063 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: MEDGEN:1714259 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: UMLS:C5234922 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MEDGEN:1714259\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0005098 {source=\"PMID:29763173\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767\"} ! stroke disorder\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9754\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060211\nname: NR5A1-related sex development disorder\ndef: \"A reproductive system disorder caused by a variation in the NR5A1 gene, and characterized by varying phenotypes, including partial or complete gonadal dysgenesis, ambiguous genitalia, and spermatogenic failure in the male, and premature ovarian failure and ovarian dysgenesis in the female.\" [https://www.clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40073/, PMID:28033660, PMID:31513305]\ncomment: 46XY individuals can present with azoospermia, hypospadias, micropenis, cryptorchidism, ambiguous or female-appearing genitalia, partial or complete gonadal dysgenesis, Sertoli dysfunction, and progressive testicular failure. Leydig function is often partially preserved, and infertility is common. 46XX individuals can present with primary ovarian insufficiency/ premature ovarian failure, ovarian dysgenesis, and subfertility. Rarely, testicular or ovotesticular disorder of sex development may occur. Individuals typically have normal adrenal function but in rare cases, adrenal insufficiency may be observed in the context of severe-early onset variants.\nsynonym: \"NR5A1-related sex development disorder\" EXACT [https://www.clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40073/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0005039 {source=\"PMID:28033660\", source=\"https://www.clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40073/\"} ! reproductive system disorder\nintersection_of: MONDO:0005039 ! reproductive system disorder\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/7983 ! NR5A1\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/7983 {source=\"PMID:28033660\"} ! NR5A1\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9863\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060212\nname: CRYAB-related myofibrillar myopathy-cataract-cardiomyopathy spectrum disorder\ndef: \"A syndromic disease caused by a variation in the CRYAB gene, and characterized by a spectrum of phenotypes including cardiomyopathy, cataract, and/or myopathy.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40151/, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2078-7280, PMID:21920752, PMID:38212463]\nsynonym: \"alpha-B crystallinopathy\" RELATED [PMID:21920752]\nsynonym: \"CRYAB-related myofibrillar myopathy-cataract-cardiomyopathy spectrum disorder\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40151/, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2078-7280] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0002254 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40151/\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2078-7280\"} ! syndromic disease\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/2389 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40151/\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2078-7280\"} ! CRYAB\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9774\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060216\nname: TSEN2-related neurodevelopmental disorder with or without thrombotic microangiopathy\ndef: \"Any neurodevelopmental disorder in which the cause of the disease is a variation in the TSEN2 gene. This condition is associated with intellectual disability, growth delay, hypotonia, motor delay, ataxia, vision issues, cardiac features (including left ventricular hypertrophy), and pulmonary complications (such as acute respiratory distress and edema). It is also linked to brain structural anomalies such as pontine and cerebellar hypoplasia, cortical atrophy, and dilated ventricles. Renal features include proteinuria, thrombotic microangiopathy, end-stage kidney disease, and high-severity hypertension.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40069/, PMID:18711368, PMID:20952379, PMID:23562994, PMID:32404165, PMID:38347586, PMID:38438125, PMID:38622473]\nsynonym: \"TSEN2-related neurodevelopmental disorder with or without thrombotic microangiopathy\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40069/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0002254 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40069/\"} ! syndromic disease\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40069/\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: MONDO:0700092 ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/28422 ! TSEN2\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/28422 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40069/\"} ! TSEN2\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9956\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:7770004\nname: CFTR-related disorder\ndef: \"A disease associated with CFTR (cystic fibrosis transmembrane conductance regulator) dysfunction that does not fulfill the diagnostic criteria for cystic fibrosis (CF). CFTR-related disorders are characterized by clinical evidence of CFTR dysfunction limited to a single organ system, a sweat chloride concentration below the CF diagnostic threshold (typically less than 60 mmol/L), and CFTR genotypes that often include at least one variant not classified as CF-causing. Recognized CFTR-related disorders include congenital bilateral absence of the vas deferens (CBAVD), acute recurrent or chronic pancreatitis, and disseminated bronchiectasis.\" [PMID:20301428, PMID:21658649]\ncomment: A CFTR-related disorder is defined as a clinical entity with evidence of CFTR dysfunction in at least one organ system that **does not meet** the diagnostic criteria for CF. Typically this means:\\n- Sweat chloride below the CF diagnostic threshold (<60 mmol/L)\\n- Clinical involvement limited to a single organ system\\n- CFTR genotype that includes at least one variant not classified as CF-causing\\n\\nSee 'cystic fibrosis' (MONDO:0009061) for diagnosis criteria for CF.\nsynonym: \"CFTR-RD\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [PMID:21658649]\nsynonym: \"CFTR-related disease\" RELATED [PMID:21658649]\nxref: MEDGEN:1854862 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: UMLS:C5924204 {source=\"MEDGEN:1854862\", source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0003847 {source=\"PMID:21658649\"} ! hereditary disease\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/1884 {source=\"PMID:21658649\"} ! CFTR\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:7770005\nname: cystic fibrosis-related liver disease\ndef: \"A liver disorder that arises as a consequence of cystic fibrosis. Cystic fibrosis-related liver disease encompasses a spectrum of hepatobiliary abnormalities caused by CFTR dysfunction in cholangiocytes, including focal biliary cirrhosis, multilobular biliary cirrhosis, hepatic steatosis, and cholangiopathy. It is a significant cause of non-pulmonary morbidity and mortality in CF, affecting approximately 5-10% of CF patients.\" [PMID:28753176, PMID:37278811]\nsynonym: \"CF liver disease\" EXACT [PMID:28753176]\nsynonym: \"CF-related liver disease\" EXACT [PMID:28753176]\nsynonym: \"CFLD\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [PMID:28753176]\nis_a: MONDO:0005154 {source=\"PMID:28753176\"} ! liver disorder\nintersection_of: MONDO:0005154 ! liver disorder\nintersection_of: disease_arises_from_feature MONDO:0009061 ! cystic fibrosis\nrelationship: disease_arises_from_feature MONDO:0009061 {source=\"PMID:28753176\"} ! cystic fibrosis\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:7770413\nname: NPY2R-related nervous system disorder, medaka\nxref: OMIA:002815-8090 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nis_a: MONDO:1011336 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! nervous system disorder, non-human animal\nrelationship: in_taxon NCBITaxon:8090 {source=\"OMIA:002815-8090\"} ! Oryzias latipes\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/10159\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:7770421\nname: DND1-related reproductive disorder, striped catfish\nxref: OMIA:002820-310915 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nis_a: MONDO:1011354 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! reproductive system disorder, non-human animal\nrelationship: in_taxon NCBITaxon:310915 {source=\"OMIA:002820-310915\"}\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/10159\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:7770472\nname: PDCD1-related immune system disorder, pig\nxref: OMIA:002851-9823 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0700106 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! immune system disorder, non-human animal\nrelationship: in_taxon NCBITaxon:9823 {source=\"OMIA:002851-9823\"} ! Sus scrofa\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/10159\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:7770496\nname: MIR137-related neurodevelopmental disorder, pig\nxref: OMIA:002860-9823 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nis_a: MONDO:1011336 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! nervous system disorder, non-human animal\nrelationship: in_taxon NCBITaxon:9823 {source=\"OMIA:002860-9823\"} ! Sus scrofa\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/10159\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:7770601\nname: patched1-related cardiovascular disorder, Nile tilapia\nxref: OMIA:002944-8128 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nis_a: MONDO:1011306 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! cardiovascular disorder, non-human animal\nrelationship: in_taxon NCBITaxon:8128 {source=\"OMIA:002944-8128\"} ! Oreochromis niloticus\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/10159\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:8000010\nname: antiphospholipid syndrome\ndef: \"A disorder caused by the presence of autoantibodies directed against phospholipids, causing a hypercoaguable state, which may result in blood clots, stroke, heart attack, and in women, significant pregnancy-related complications, including miscarriage and still birth. The syndrome is often associated with other autoimmune disorders, most commonly lupus erythematosus, and infections, including syphilis and Lyme disease.\" [NCIT:C61283]\nsubset: doid {source=\"DOID:2988\"}\nsubset: doid_rare {source=\"DOID:2988\"}\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0005824\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: ncit {source=\"NCIT:C61283\"}\nsubset: ordo_disorder {source=\"Orphanet:80\"}\nsubset: orphanet {source=\"Orphanet:80\"}\nsubset: orphanet_rare {source=\"Orphanet:80\"}\nsubset: otar {source=\"MONDO:OTAR\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"antiphospholipid antibody syndrome\" EXACT [DOID:2988, ICD10CM:D68.61, NCIT:C61283, Orphanet:80]\nsynonym: \"antiphospholipid syndrome\" EXACT [DOID:2988, ICD10CM:D68.61, icd11.foundation:1173370808, NCIT:C61283, Orphanet:80]\nsynonym: \"familial lupus anticoagulant\" EXACT []\nsynonym: \"Hughes syndrome\" EXACT [icd11.foundation:1173370808, Orphanet:80]\nxref: DOID:2988 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: EFO:0002689 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:EFO\"}\nxref: GARD:0005824 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nxref: ICD10CM:D68.61 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"DOID:2988\"}\nxref: icd11.foundation:1173370808 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"Orphanet:80\"}\nxref: ICD9:279.49 {source=\"MONDO:relatedTo\", source=\"MONDO:i2s\"}\nxref: MEDGEN:38834 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: MESH:D016736 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"DOID:2988\"}\nxref: NCIT:C61283 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"DOID:2988\"}\nxref: Orphanet:80 {source=\"OMIM:107320\", source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: SCTID:19267009 {source=\"DOID:2988\"}\nxref: SCTID:201450008 {source=\"DOID:2988\"}\nxref: SCTID:26843008 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"DOID:2988\"}\nxref: UMLS:C0085278 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\", source=\"MEDGEN:38834\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0002254 {source=\"NCIT:C61283\"} ! syndromic disease\nis_a: MONDO:0007179 {source=\"DOID:2988\", source=\"MESH:D016736\"} ! autoimmune disease\nrelationship: disease_has_feature HP:0001977 {source=\"NCIT:C61283\"} ! Abnormal thrombosis\nproperty_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/antiphospholipid_syndrome\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432\n\n","metadata":{"output":"...\n\nhub.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9063\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060148\nname: empty nose syndrome\ndef: \"A rare iatrogenic disease characterized by paradoxical nasal obstruction and symptoms including air hunger and suffocation-like breathing sensation, nasal dryness and crusting, burning pain or cold airflow sensation, impaired sleep and cognitive function and severe anxiety and depression, and typically occurs after surgical reduction or removal of nasal turbinates.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163, PMID:27557473, PMID:39126290]\ncomment: ENS is often misdiagnosed as psychiatric in origin due to the disproportionate suffering compared to physical exam findings. ENS results from disruption of normal nasal airflow dynamics, mucosal sensory feedback, and humidification, typically after aggressive surgical intervention on the nasal turbinates. Estimated prevalence: <1 in 10,000, though underreporting and misdiagnosis likely make this an underestimate. ENS is currently considered a rare, post-surgical complication, with cases reported globally but concentrated among ENT surgical patients. No universally accepted biomarker exists. Diagnosis is based on symptoms, medical history and imaging. There is no cure. Symptom management includes nasal moisturization (saline gels, humidification), nerve modulating agents (e.g., amitriptyline, gabapentin) nasal implants to restore airflow resistance and cognitive-behavioral therapy and psychiatric support. ENS most often develops after surgery and is considered an iatrogenic condition because its other causes also result from medical interventions, such as electrocautery or laser procedures that cause turbinate trauma.\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028165\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: mondo_curated_rare {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\", source=\"PMID:35155777\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"ENS\" EXACT [PMID:27557473, PMID:39126290]\nsynonym: \"nasal iatrogenic dysfunction\" BROAD [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163]\nsynonym: \"post-turbinectomy syndrome\" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163, PMID:17875850]\nsynonym: \"secondary atrophic rhinitis\" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163, PMID:35155777]\nxref: GARD:0028165 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nxref: MEDGEN:1876481 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: UMLS:C3888849 {source=\"MEDGEN:1876481\", source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0005659 {source=\"PMID:35155777\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163\"} ! atrophic rhinitis\nis_a: MONDO:0043543 {source=\"PMID:17875850\", source=\"PMID:27557473\", source=\"PMID:38961700\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163\"} ! iatrogenic disease\nrelationship: excluded_from_qc_check http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/mondo/sparql/qc/general/qc-single-child.sparql\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9174\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060149\nname: ACAN-related short stature spectrum\ndef: \"A rare semidominant genetic skeletal disorder caused by a variation in ACAN gene, characterized by short stature with variable phenotypic features which may include osteochondritis dissecans, advanced bone age, early-onset arthritis, and/or features consistent with spondyloepiphyseal dysplasia, Kimberley type caused by a single allele whereas biallelic variation can cause spondyloepimetaphyseal dysplasia, aggrecan type.\" [PMID:27311816, PMID:35434101]\nis_a: MONDO:0005381 {source=\"PMID:35434101\"} ! bone disorder\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/319 {source=\"PMID:35434101\"} ! ACAN\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9249\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060150\nname: NOTCH1-related AOS spectrum disorder\ndef: \"A disease characterized by a spectrum of cardiac and extracardiac phenotypes caused by a disease-causing variant in the NOTCH1 gene, inherited in an autosomal dominant manner. Affected individuals may present with congenital heart defects, bicuspid aortic valve, aortic valve stenosis, thoracic aortic aneurysm or dissection, anomalies in brain structure, intracranial or posterior circulation vascular anomalies, cutaneous vascular malformations, cutis marmorata, and/or a phenotype compatible with Adams-Oliver syndrome (i.e. cutis aplasia, terminal limb defects, skull ossification defects).\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40104/, https://orcid.org/0009-0007-6180-2639, PMID:25963545]\ncomment: Variants in NOTCH1 have been reported in individuals with the following disease entities: Adams-Oliver Syndrome, congenital heart disease, aortic valve disease including bicuspid aortic valve, and thoracic aortic aneurysm and dissection. Individuals with pathogenic variants in NOTCH1 may also be asymptomatic due to incomplete penetrance and extensive intrafamilial variability. Per criteria outlined by the ClinGen Lumping and Splitting guidelines, we found no difference in molecular mechanism and inheritance pattern and found considerable interfamilial and intrafamilial variability in cardiac phenotypes. Therefore, Adams-Oliver syndrome 5 and aortic valve disease 1 have been lumped into one disease entity (NOTCH1-related AOS spectrum disorder).\nis_a: MONDO:0002254 {source=\"PMID:25963545\", source=\"PMID:38778082\"} ! syndromic disease\nis_a: MONDO:0005453 {source=\"PMID:38778082\", source=\"PMID:40127276\", source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40104/\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0009-0007-6180-2639\"} ! congenital heart disease\nrelationship: has_characteristic HP:0000006 {source=\"PMID:25963545\", source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40104/\"} ! Autosomal dominant inheritance\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/7881 {source=\"PMID:25963545\", source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40104/\"} ! NOTCH1\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9236\" xsd:string\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9832\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060165\nname: ELANE-related neutropenia\ndef: \"Any neutropenia in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the ELANE gene.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163, MONDO:patterns/disease_series_by_gene]\ncomment: ELANE-related neutropenia includes congenital neutropenia and cyclic neutropenia, both of which are primary hematologic disorders characterized by recurrent fever, skin and oropharyngeal inflammation (i.e., mouth ulcers, gingivitis, sinusitis, and pharyngitis), and cervical adenopathy. Infectious complications are generally more severe in congenital neutropenia than in cyclic neutropenia.\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028170\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nxref: GARD:0028170 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0001475 {source=\"PMID:20301705\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163\"} ! neutropenia\nintersection_of: MONDO:0001475 ! neutropenia\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/3309 ! ELANE\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/3309 {source=\"PMID:20301705\"} ! ELANE\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9459\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060173\nname: FLNB-associated autosomal dominant filamin related bone disorder\ndef: \"Any autosomal dominant filamin related bone disorder in which the cause of the disease is a variation in FLNB gene.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40106/, MONDO:patterns/disease_series_by_gene, PMID:16752402, PMID:16801345, PMID:22190451, PMID:22354125]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028175\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"FLNB-associated autosomal dominant filamin related bone disorder\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40106/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nxref: GARD:0028175 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0000426 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40106/\"} ! autosomal dominant disease\nis_a: MONDO:0019690 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40106/\"} ! filamin-related bone disorder\nintersection_of: MONDO:0000426 ! autosomal dominant disease\nintersection_of: MONDO:0019690 ! filamin-related bone disorder\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/3755 ! FLNB\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/3755 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40106/\"} ! FLNB\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9528\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060179\nname: RNU5B-1 related neurodevelopmental disorder with seizures and joint laxity\ndef: \"A neurodevelopmental disorder in which the cause of the disease is a variation in RNU5B-1 gene and is characterized by global developmental delay, hypotonia, macrocephaly, failure to thrive, abnormality of the eye, seizures, and joint laxity\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40060/, MONDO:patterns/disease_series_by_gene, PMID:40379786, PMID:40442284]\nsubset: omim {source=\"OMIM:621302\"}\nsynonym: \"NEDSJL\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [OMIM:621302]\nsynonym: \"neurodevelopmental disorder with seizures and joint laxity\" EXACT [OMIM:621302]\nsynonym: \"RNU5B-1 related neurodevelopmental disorder with seizures and joint laxity\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40060/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nsynonym: \"RNU5B-1-related disorder\" BROAD [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40060/]\nxref: OMIM:621302 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0100500 {source=\"PMID:40379786\", source=\"PMID:40442284\", source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40060/\"} ! Mendelian neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: MONDO:0100500 ! Mendelian neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/10212 ! RNU5B-1\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/10212 {source=\"OMIM:621302\", source=\"PMID:40379786\", source=\"PMID:40442284\", source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40060/\"} ! RNU5B-1\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator \"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\" xsd:string\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9596\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060190\nname: APP-related brain and vascular amyloidosis\ndef: \"A hereditary amyloidosis characterized by a spectrum of neurodegenerative and neurovascular phenotypes caused by pathogenic variant in the APP gene, resulting in an abnormal clearance of amyloid peptides, either by overproduction and decreased clearance of amyloid peptides, with deposition of amyloid in plaques and blood vessel walls. Affected individuals may present with progressive cognitive decline, cerebral vascular amyloidosis with white matter changes, and stroke with or without hemorrhage.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40156/]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028185\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"APP-related brain and vascular amyloidosis\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40156/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nxref: GARD:0028185 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0011057 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40156/\"} ! cerebrovascular disorder\nis_a: MONDO:0018634 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40156/\"} ! hereditary amyloidosis\nis_a: MONDO:0024237 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40156/\"} ! inherited neurodegenerative disorder\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/620 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40156/\"} ! APP\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9721\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060192\nname: CASK-related intellectual disability\ndef: \"A syndromic disorder in which the cause of the disease is a variation in the CASK gene. It is associated with a wide phenotypic spectrum ranging from mild-to-severe intellectual disability with or without nystagmus to moderate-to-profound intellectual disability and progressive microcephaly with pontine and cerebellar hypoplasia, often associated with seizures.\" [MONDO:patterns/disease_series_by_gene, PMID:24278995]\nsynonym: \"CASK-related disorder\" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163, PMID:24278995]\nis_a: MONDO:0002254 {source=\"PMID:24278995\"} ! syndromic disease\nis_a: MONDO:0020119 {source=\"PMID:24278995\"} ! X-linked syndromic intellectual disability\nintersection_of: MONDO:0000508 ! syndromic intellectual disability\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/1497 ! CASK\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9747\" xsd:string\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060194\nname: FAS-related autoimmune lymphoproliferative immune disorder\ndef: \"An autoimmune lymphoproliferative syndrome that results from defective lymphocyte homoestasis, and is caused by variants in the FAS gene. It is characterized by non-malignant lymphoproliferation, autoimmune disease, and lifelong increased risk for both Hodgkin and non-Hodgkin lymphoma.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028187\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"FAS-related autoimmune lymphoproliferative immune disorder\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nxref: GARD:0028187 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0017979 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! autoimmune lymphoproliferative syndrome\nintersection_of: MONDO:0017979 ! autoimmune lymphoproliferative syndrome\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/11920 ! FAS\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/11920 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! FAS\nrelationship: predisposes_towards MONDO:0004952 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! Hodgkins lymphoma\nrelationship: predisposes_towards MONDO:0018908 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! non-Hodgkin lymphoma\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9749\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060195\nname: SH2B3-related immune system disorder\ndef: \"A predisposition caused by a mutation in SH2B3 gene that presents with myeloproliferation and/or multi-organ autoimmunity.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/]\nsynonym: \"SH2B3-related immune system disorder\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nsynonym: \"SH2B3-related myeloproliferation and autoimmunity\" RELATED [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/]\nis_a: MONDO:0020573 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! inherited disease susceptibility\nintersection_of: MONDO:0020573 ! inherited disease susceptibility\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/29605 ! SH2B3\nintersection_of: predisposes_towards MONDO:0005046 ! immune system disorder\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/29605 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! SH2B3\nrelationship: predisposes_towards MONDO:0005046 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40157/\"} ! immune system disorder\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9576\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060199\nname: hemorrhagic stroke\ndef: \"A stroke disorder caused by bleeding into the brain parenchyma or surrounding spaces. Hemorrhagic stroke includes intracerebral hemorrhage (bleeding within the brain tissue) and subarachnoid hemorrhage (bleeding in the space between the brain and the surrounding membrane).\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767, https://www.hopkinsmedicine.org/health/conditions-and-diseases/stroke/types-of-stroke, https://www.stroke.org.uk/stroke/types, PMID:29763173]\nsubset: doid {source=\"DOID:0051063\"}\nsynonym: \"haemorrhagic stroke\" EXACT OMO:0003005 []\nxref: DOID:0051063 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: MEDGEN:1714259 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: UMLS:C5234922 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MEDGEN:1714259\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0005098 {source=\"PMID:29763173\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1149-7767\"} ! stroke disorder\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9754\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060211\nname: NR5A1-related sex development disorder\ndef: \"A reproductive system disorder caused by a variation in the NR5A1 gene, and characterized by varying phenotypes, including partial or complete gonadal dysgenesis, ambiguous genitalia, and spermatogenic failure in the male, and premature ovarian failure and ovarian dysgenesis in the female.\" [https://www.clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40073/, PMID:28033660, PMID:31513305]\ncomment: 46XY individuals can present with azoospermia, hypospadias, micropenis, cryptorchidism, ambiguous or female-appearing genitalia, partial or complete gonadal dysgenesis, Sertoli dysfunction, and progressive testicular failure. Leydig function is often partially preserved, and infertility is common. 46XX individuals can present with primary ovarian insufficiency/ premature ovarian failure, ovarian dysgenesis, and subfertility. Rarely, testicular or ovotesticular disorder of sex development may occur. Individuals typically have normal adrenal function but in rare cases, adrenal insufficiency may be observed in the context of severe-early onset variants.\nsynonym: \"NR5A1-related sex development disorder\" EXACT [https://www.clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40073/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0005039 {source=\"PMID:28033660\", source=\"https://www.clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40073/\"} ! reproductive system disorder\nintersection_of: MONDO:0005039 ! reproductive system disorder\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/7983 ! NR5A1\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/7983 {source=\"PMID:28033660\"} ! NR5A1\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9863\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060212\nname: CRYAB-related myofibrillar myopathy-cataract-cardiomyopathy spectrum disorder\ndef: \"A syndromic disease caused by a variation in the CRYAB gene, and characterized by a spectrum of phenotypes including cardiomyopathy, cataract, and/or myopathy.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40151/, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2078-7280, PMID:21920752, PMID:38212463]\nsynonym: \"alpha-B crystallinopathy\" RELATED [PMID:21920752]\nsynonym: \"CRYAB-related myofibrillar myopathy-cataract-cardiomyopathy spectrum disorder\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40151/, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2078-7280] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0002254 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40151/\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2078-7280\"} ! syndromic disease\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/2389 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40151/\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2078-7280\"} ! CRYAB\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9774\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060216\nname: TSEN2-related neurodevelopmental disorder with or without thrombotic microangiopathy\ndef: \"Any neurodevelopmental disorder in which the cause of the disease is a variation in the TSEN2 gene. This condition is associated with intellectual disability, growth delay, hypotonia, motor delay, ataxia, vision issues, cardiac features (including left ventricular hypertrophy), and pulmonary complications (such as acute respiratory distress and edema). It is also linked to brain structural anomalies such as pontine and cerebellar hypoplasia, cortical atrophy, and dilated ventricles. Renal features include proteinuria, thrombotic microangiopathy, end-stage kidney disease, and high-severity hypertension.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40069/, PMID:18711368, PMID:20952379, PMID:23562994, PMID:32404165, PMID:38347586, PMID:38438125, PMID:38622473]\nsynonym: \"TSEN2-related neurodevelopmental disorder with or without thrombotic microangiopathy\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40069/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0002254 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40069/\"} ! syndromic disease\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40069/\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: MONDO:0700092 ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/28422 ! TSEN2\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/28422 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40069/\"} ! TSEN2\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9956\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:7770004\nname: CFTR-related disorder\ndef: \"A disease associated with CFTR (cystic fibrosis transmembrane conductance regulator) dysfunction that does not fulfill the diagnostic criteria for cystic fibrosis (CF). CFTR-related disorders are characterized by clinical evidence of CFTR dysfunction limited to a single organ system, a sweat chloride concentration below the CF diagnostic threshold (typically less than 60 mmol/L), and CFTR genotypes that often include at least one variant not classified as CF-causing. Recognized CFTR-related disorders include congenital bilateral absence of the vas deferens (CBAVD), acute recurrent or chronic pancreatitis, and disseminated bronchiectasis.\" [PMID:20301428, PMID:21658649]\ncomment: A CFTR-related disorder is defined as a clinical entity with evidence of CFTR dysfunction in at least one organ system that **does not meet** the diagnostic criteria for CF. Typically this means:\\n- Sweat chloride below the CF diagnostic threshold (<60 mmol/L)\\n- Clinical involvement limited to a single organ system\\n- CFTR genotype that includes at least one variant not classified as CF-causing\\n\\nSee 'cystic fibrosis' (MONDO:0009061) for diagnosis criteria for CF.\nsynonym: \"CFTR-RD\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [PMID:21658649]\nsynonym: \"CFTR-related disease\" RELATED [PMID:21658649]\nxref: MEDGEN:1854862 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: UMLS:C5924204 {source=\"MEDGEN:1854862\", source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0003847 {source=\"PMID:21658649\"} ! hereditary disease\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/1884 {source=\"PMID:21658649\"} ! CFTR\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:7770005\nname: cystic fibrosis-related liver disease\ndef: \"A liver disorder that arises as a consequence of cystic fibrosis. Cystic fibrosis-related liver disease encompasses a spectrum of hepatobiliary abnormalities caused by CFTR dysfunction in cholangiocytes, including focal biliary cirrhosis, multilobular biliary cirrhosis, hepatic steatosis, and cholangiopathy. It is a significant cause of non-pulmonary morbidity and mortality in CF, affecting approximately 5-10% of CF patients.\" [PMID:28753176, PMID:37278811]\nsynonym: \"CF liver disease\" EXACT [PMID:28753176]\nsynonym: \"CF-related liver disease\" EXACT [PMID:28753176]\nsynonym: \"CFLD\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [PMID:28753176]\nis_a: MONDO:0005154 {source=\"PMID:28753176\"} ! liver disorder\nintersection_of: MONDO:0005154 ! liver disorder\nintersection_of: disease_arises_from_feature MONDO:0009061 ! cystic fibrosis\nrelationship: disease_arises_from_feature MONDO:0009061 {source=\"PMID:28753176\"} ! cystic fibrosis\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:7770413\nname: NPY2R-related nervous system disorder, medaka\nxref: OMIA:002815-8090 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nis_a: MONDO:1011336 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! nervous system disorder, non-human animal\nrelationship: in_taxon NCBITaxon:8090 {source=\"OMIA:002815-8090\"} ! Oryzias latipes\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/10159\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:7770421\nname: DND1-related reproductive disorder, striped catfish\nxref: OMIA:002820-310915 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nis_a: MONDO:1011354 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! reproductive system disorder, non-human animal\nrelationship: in_taxon NCBITaxon:310915 {source=\"OMIA:002820-310915\"}\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/10159\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:7770472\nname: PDCD1-related immune system disorder, pig\nxref: OMIA:002851-9823 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0700106 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! immune system disorder, non-human animal\nrelationship: in_taxon NCBITaxon:9823 {source=\"OMIA:002851-9823\"} ! Sus scrofa\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/10159\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:7770496\nname: MIR137-related neurodevelopmental disorder, pig\nxref: OMIA:002860-9823 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nis_a: MONDO:1011336 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! nervous system disorder, non-human animal\nrelationship: in_taxon NCBITaxon:9823 {source=\"OMIA:002860-9823\"} ! Sus scrofa\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/10159\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:7770601\nname: patched1-related cardiovascular disorder, Nile tilapia\nxref: OMIA:002944-8128 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nis_a: MONDO:1011306 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! cardiovascular disorder, non-human animal\nrelationship: in_taxon NCBITaxon:8128 {source=\"OMIA:002944-8128\"} ! Oreochromis niloticus\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/10159\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:8000010\nname: antiphospholipid syndrome\ndef: \"A disorder caused by the presence of autoantibodies directed against phospholipids, causing a hypercoaguable state, which may result in blood clots, stroke, heart attack, and in women, significant pregnancy-related complications, including miscarriage and still birth. The syndrome is often associated with other autoimmune disorders, most commonly lupus erythematosus, and infections, including syphilis and Lyme disease.\" [NCIT:C61283]\nsubset: doid {source=\"DOID:2988\"}\nsubset: doid_rare {source=\"DOID:2988\"}\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0005824\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: ncit {source=\"NCIT:C61283\"}\nsubset: ordo_disorder {source=\"Orphanet:80\"}\nsubset