quested RNU12-related disease spectrum and reclassifying existing child terms under it.\n+\n+Changes made:\n+- Added new term `MONDO:7770747` `RNU12-related minor spliceopathy disorder`.\n+- Added a definition citing the peer-reviewed publication `PMID:40975062`.\n+- Added `has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in` for `RNU12` using `HGNC:19380`.\n+- Added issue tracking metadata for `https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9963`.\n+- Reclassified these existing terms as children of the new umbrella term without removing any existing parents:\n+  - `MONDO:0011287` `craniosynostosis-anal anomalies-porokeratosis syndrome`\n+  - `MONDO:0859360` `spinocerebellar ataxia, autosomal recessive 33`\n+  - `MONDO:0033717` `congenital cerebellar ataxia due to RNU12 mutation`\n+\n+Rationale:\n+- The issue requested a spectrum-level term for RNU12-associated minor spliceopathy and explicitly identified `MONDO:0011287` and `MONDO:0859360` as children.\n+- There was already a third existing RNU12-associated ataxia term in MONDO (`MONDO:0033717`), so I also classified that term under the new spectrum umbrella to keep the hierarchy internally consistent.\n+- I retained the existing asserted parents on all child terms and only added the new parent, following MONDO guidance for adding more specific parentage.\n+\n+Validation and background checks completed:\n+- Read the imported issue context from `__issue_context__.json`.\n+- Checked the cited publication and used the peer-reviewed update `PMID:40975062` instead of the preprint-only citation when building the new definition.\n+- Verified the existing `RNU12` gene identifier in MONDO usage as `http://identifiers.org/hgnc/19380`.\n+- Checked the existing MONDO hierarchy for the requested child terms and for other spectrum/gene-related umbrella terms.\n+- Ran local syntax validation with:\n+  - `robot convert --catalog src/ontology/catalog-v001.xml -i src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo -f obo -o /tmp/opencode/mondo-edit.TMP.obo`\n+